 a standard research tool in many disciplines including Molecular Ecology, but the rapid technological advances in combination with several competing platforms have resulted in a confusing diversity of formats. This lack of standard formats causes several problems, such as undocumented preprocessing steps or the loss of information in downstream software tools, which do not account for the specifics of the different available formats. ReadTools is an open-source Java toolkit designed to standardize and preprocess read data from different platforms. It manages FASTQ- and SAM-formatted inputs while dealing with platform-specific peculiarities and provides a standard SAM compliant output. The code and executable are available at https://github.com/magicDGS/ReadTools.","authors":[{"name":"Gomez-Sanchez D."},{"name":"Schlotterer C."}],"citationCount":23,"date":"2018-05-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Molecular Ecology Resources","title":"ReadTools: A universal toolkit for handling sequence data from different sequencing platforms"},"pmid":"29171165","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Genomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0622"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"ReadTools","home":"https://bio.tools/readtools","license":"MIT","summary":"ReadTools is an open\u2010source toolkit designed to standardize and preprocess sequencing read data from different platforms. It manages FASTQ\u2010 and SAM\u2010formatted inputs while dealing with platform\u2010specific peculiarities and provides a standard SAM compliant output.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:readtools/cmd/magicdgs.github.io","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"fre